# The program's own way through the records: k = 2, always the top, fan 4,096 on a hop and 512 on a search, 8 hops,
# lambda = 0.05 (Semantics: Personality firmware, "One set of decisions").
#
# A firmware is one human being's selection: how the records are navigated and how an answer is reached. It is a
# file, never a record, so it does not contaminate the knowledge; the same records can be pulled under another.
# Every line is one decision. The decisions a line can make:
#
#   k N                        how far below its rating a standing must still hold, in deviations
#   lambda N                   the tax on another hop
#   fan N                      how many claims that hold an entity are read; one that holds more is reached, not crossed
#   hops N                     how many hops a chain may run
#   top always | within N      whether the top of a set is taken every time, or how near a tie has to be before
#                              another strand can be taken (the temperature of that choice)
#   refuse predicate NAME...   kinds of strand refused before they are scored
#   refuse witness NAME...
#   fact N                     a member of the set curated by a witness of at least this trust is returned as one
#                              fact, the rest of the set held back; without the line, no such branch fires
#   order witness | standing   on a claim with a part left open: the witness's own order before the standing, or not
#   weigh N KIND...            role weights: strands of these kinds pull N as hard (0 to 1; 1 unless said). A weight is
#                              the firmware's reading, never a change to a standing
#   role by KIND               how hard a word pulls is read from what is attested of it under KIND (its part of speech)
#   role N VALUE...            a word of that VALUE pulls N as hard (0 to 1)
#   shape frechet | outliers N | dtw | edr N
#                              which shape of the tree to favor, and how many variable vertices a match may skip
#
# An instruction set takes the steps of one operation of the forward pass: "for OPERATION", then the decisions that
# hold for it, and for a pull the segments a step takes, in order:
#
#   take fact                  the single fact, when the branch above fires
#   take segment               the rest of the branch the prompt is a run of, followed along what was observed
#   take attestations N        the N strongest strands of the prompt itself
#   take constituents N        the N strongest strands of each of its constituents
#   take chain N RELATION...   from each of the N words that pull hardest, the relations followed in order, each by its
#                              witness's order then its standing: where the chain ends is the answer. Chains
#                              parted by | are tried in turn until one reaches its end (a form through its lemma)
k 2
lambda 0.05
hops 8
top always
order witness

# Role weights, as drafted by hand (Semantics: Personality firmware, "Weights that are not standings"; Research: Trust):
# the relations that carry what a sentence is about pull hardest, and the function-word relations a fraction as hard,
# so filler does not drown everything.
weigh 0.9 nsubj obj
weigh 0.8 iobj csubj ccomp compound flat
weigh 0.7 obl nmod appos
weigh 0.6 amod conj
weigh 0.5 advmod
weigh 0.2 aux cop discourse
weigh 0.15 case mark
weigh 0.1 det cc
weigh 0.05 punct
# What a treebank says of a word's form (its tags, lemma and morphological features) is grammar, not what the word
# is about: weighed with the function-word relations. The program's default; another firmware weighs otherwise.
weigh 0.1 UPOS XPOS LEMMA FEATS MISC SpaceAfter Number Tense PronType Mood VerbForm Person Case Gender Definite Degree Poss Reflex NumType Voice Aspect Polarity Abbr Foreign Typo Animacy

# How hard a word pulls, by its part of speech, as drafted by hand (Research: Trust, role trust): a name or a noun
# carries what a sentence is about; a determiner, an auxiliary or a pronoun a fraction of it.
role by UPOS
role 1 PROPN
role 0.9 NOUN
role 0.8 VERB
role 0.7 ADJ NUM
role 0.5 ADV
role 0.3 PRON INTJ SYM
role 0.2 AUX SCONJ X
role 0.15 ADP
role 0.1 DET CCONJ PART
role 0.05 PUNCT

for hop
  fan 4096

for search
  fan 512

for translate
  fan 4096

for pull
  fan 4096
  # strands of a kind the pull does not navigate (Sequence: Web 15.x): a sentence's tag layers and an example's marked
  # arguments pull back their tags, not what the sentence is about. A default to be ruled on; the firmware is the inventor's.
  refuse predicate BNC PENN GF PT NER WSL Target Other Sent Verb Noun Adj Prep Adv UPOS XPOS DEPREL FEATS MISC LEMMA type n f itype
  take chain 1 Sense Definition | LEMMA Sense Definition
  take segment
  take attestations 3
  take constituents 1
